<title>USA: Penn Traffic Co Q3 loss widens.</title>
<headline>Penn Traffic Co Q3 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>SYRACUSE, N.Y. 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands of dollars, except per share data)</p>
<p>			     Thirteen Wks	   Thirteen Wks</p>
<p>					Ended		   Ended</p>
<p>			    Nov. 2, 1996	   Oct. 28, 1995</p>
<p> Total Revenues		$811,125		 $844,619</p>
<p> Operating income		10,805		   29,637</p>
<p> Net (loss)		   ( 15,924)		   ( 350)</p>
<p> Shr (loss)		     ( 1.46)		  ( 0.03)</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    10,869,441	     10,867,977</p>
<p>			  Thirty-nine Wks	Thirty-nine Wks</p>
<p>				     Ended		    Ended</p>
<p>			    Nov. 2, 1996	   Oct. 28, 1995</p>
<p> Total Revenues	    $2,481,547	     $2,588,876</p>
<p> Operating income		52,475		   31,349</p>
<p> Net (loss)		   ( 35,102)		( 51,925)</p>
<p> Shr (loss)		     ( 3.23)		  ( 4.78)</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    10,863,407	     10,861,394</p>
<p>NOTE: During the second quarter of Fiscal 1996, the company recorded expenses totaling $65.2 million ($51.9 million net of tax benefit) related to the closure of the stand-alone general merchandise business (Harts), the write-off of equipment, the company's expense reduction program and an increase in the company's closed store reserve.</p>
<p>Current Q3 hurt by $2.5 million by work stoppage at Sani-Dairy division.</p>
